+"""
+test_backend_parity_exhaustive.py
+=================================
+Every public symbol that exists in *both* backends, driven in both and compared.
+
+Why this file exists
+--------------------
+``cool_frames.torch`` is not a wrapper around ``cool_frames.numpy``.  Roughly
+2,400 of its 6,500 lines are independent reimplementations — ``core/_core.py``
+(858 lines), ``filterbanks/_core.py`` (487), ``phase/_fbphasegradfrommag.py``
+(373), ``phase/_spsi.py`` (255), ``filters/_biquad.py`` (233),
+``diagnostics/spectrogram.py`` (181).  Two implementations of the same
+mathematics, maintained by hand, with nothing comparing them.
+
+The consequence is the defining pattern of this audit: **a defect gets fixed
+where it was noticed, and nowhere else.**  Before this file there were five
+recorded instances —
+
+1. ``real=False`` as a default: NumPy ``filterbankiter``, then torch
+   ``filterbankiter``, then NumPy ``ifilterbankiter``, and finally torch
+   ``ifilterbankiter``, which went on reconstructing the flagship bank with
+   23 % error through all three of the other fixes.
+2. The missing centre-frequency term in the phase-gradient estimator: fixed in
+   NumPy, left in torch for a whole release.
+3. ``_winwidthatheight``'s DFT-ordering assumption: fixed in
+   ``numpy/filters/_gabfilters.py``, left in ``numpy/phase/_findgamma.py``,
+   where it made ``pghi_findgamma`` 6-10x wrong for any numeric window.
+
+— and writing this harness immediately produced three more, all in torch code
+that no test had ever compared against its NumPy twin:
+
+4. ``spsi``'s phase accumulator ran in **float32**.  ``2.0 * torch.pi * a[m]``
+   with an int32 ``a`` promotes to the *default* dtype, not the resolved one,
+   so the product was rounded to single precision before meeting the float64
+   instantaneous frequency.  7.7e-8 rad of error on the first frame, 7.3e-6 by
+   frame 63, in a function whose signature and resolved dtype both say float64.
+5. ``reassigned_spectrogram`` had ``tgrad`` and ``fgrad`` **swapped** in its
+   return dict, so ``instfreq_deviation`` reported the group delay and
+   ``groupdelay_shift`` reported the instantaneous frequency — off by a factor
+   of ``fs/2pi`` as well.  The NumPy copy carries a comment describing this
+   exact defect being fixed *there*.  It also dropped ``L`` from both the
+   analysis and gradient calls, wrapped the gradient call in a bare
+   ``except Exception -> zeros``, padded the dB image at 0.0 dB (i.e. magnitude
+   1.0, which then won the ``peak_db`` maximum), hardcoded the clip level to
+   60, and omitted the ``db_range`` parameter its NumPy twin has always had.
+6. ``filterbank_spectrogram`` shared the 0.0-dB padding and the dropped ``L``.
+
+Six for six.  The pattern is not going to stop being true on its own, so the
+harness is built to be *self-maintaining* rather than a list somebody has to
+remember to extend:
+
+* ``test_public_surface_divergence_is_recorded`` enumerates both backends and
+  fails if the set of names present in one and not the other changes.  Add a
+  function to NumPy and forget torch, and this fails.
+* ``test_every_shared_symbol_has_a_parity_driver`` fails if a shared symbol has
+  no entry in ``DRIVERS``.  Add a function to *both* backends and forget to say
+  how to compare them, and this fails.
+* ``test_backends_agree`` is parametrised over ``DRIVERS`` and does the actual
+  comparison.
+
+The two enforcement tests are the point.  Without them this file is a snapshot
+that rots; with them it is a constraint on the codebase.
+"""
